          <h2>The benefit categories behind WellFinder treatments</h2>
          <p>Green Shield group plans pay for most wellness care through paramedical benefits. The category follows the provider designation, meaning the profession of the person who treated you. When you claim online, Green Shield asks you to select the paramedical service type that matches that designation, so the words on your receipt matter. The categories that matter most for WellFinder readers are:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Physiotherapy, which covers pelvic floor physiotherapy, vestibular rehabilitation and shockwave therapy</li>
            <li>Osteopathy, which covers facial manual therapy and some pressotherapy clinics that bill through an osteopathic practitioner</li>
            <li>Massage therapy, which covers TMJ massage, lymphatic drainage and head spa treatments given by a registered massage therapist</li>
            <li>Chiropractic, which some clinical Pilates and golf assessment clinics bill under</li>
            <li>Naturopathy, which covers microneedling, IV and IM vitamin therapy and fertility consultations with a naturopathic doctor</li>
            <li>Acupuncture, which covers fertility acupuncture, cosmetic acupuncture and facial gua sha from a registered acupuncturist</li>
            <li>Psychology and counselling, which cover couples therapy, sleep coaching and mental performance coaching</li>
            <li>Speech therapy, which covers singing voice therapy, accent modification and stuttering therapy</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Your plan decides which categories you hold, the annual maximum for each and the amount paid per visit. Green Shield plans commonly work with combined maximums for some services and separate maximums for others. A provider also needs to be registered with Green Shield for online claiming.</p>

          <h2>How claiming works with Green Shield</h2>
          <p>Members register for GreenShield+, the member site and app, to claim online. Many online claims for paramedical services are adjudicated in real time, so you learn how much your plan covers as soon as the claim is assessed. Green Shield member materials also describe a pretend claim feature, which lets you enter a sample expense and see what portion your plan would cover before you spend anything. To claim well:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Register for GreenShield+ and set up direct deposit, so payments go straight to your bank account</li>
            <li>Keep the receipt from every visit, showing the provider, their designation, the date and the amount paid</li>
            <li>Choose the paramedical service type that matches your provider designation when you submit</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Direct billing is widely offered under Green Shield plans. Many health providers submit the claim electronically on your behalf at the visit, and you pay only the part your plan leaves with you. Providers bill through Green Shield's own provider system, so a clinic that direct bills another insurer may still need to register separately for Green Shield. Ask when you book.</p>
          <p>Paper claims remain available for services that cannot be claimed online, using the claim form for your plan.</p>

          <h2>Health care and personal spending accounts</h2>
          <p>Many Green Shield plans include a Health Care Spending Account, often shortened to HCSA. The account holds credits from your employer for eligible health and dental expenses, following the list the Canada Revenue Agency allows, and members can claim those expenses online through GreenShield+ like any other claim. Some Green Shield plans also include a Personal Spending Account, or PSA, for wellness costs your employer chooses to allow, and members can view HCSA and PSA balances in their account.</p>
          <p>The usual order is main plan first, then the spending account for what remains. Account amounts, eligible items and deadlines are set in your plan, and Green Shield member guidance generally asks members to submit expenses within 12 months of the date of service unless the plan states a different rule.</p>

          <h2>WellFinder treatments and how they may bill under a Green Shield plan</h2>
          <p>Costs below are typical Canadian prices collected for the WellFinder directory. Your plan pays according to its own maximums, so confirm the amounts for each category in GreenShield+.</p>
