          <h2>Questions members ask</h2>
          <h3>Does Green Shield cover osteopathy?</h3>
          <p>Many Green Shield group plans include osteopathy as a paramedical category. Coverage depends on your plan including the category and on the practitioner being registered, so confirm both in GreenShield+ before your first visit.</p>
          <h3>What is a pretend claim?</h3>
          <p>It is a trial claim inside Green Shield member services. You enter the service and the amount, and the tool shows what portion your plan would cover, based on your remaining balances and plan rules. Members use it to test a larger expense before committing to the cost.</p>
          <h3>Can my provider bill Green Shield directly?</h3>
          <p>Many can. Providers registered with Green Shield submit claims electronically at the visit, and you present your benefits card so they have the numbers they need. If your provider is not registered, you pay at the visit and claim online yourself with the receipt.</p>
          <h3>Why was my service type rejected online?</h3>
          <p>The usual cause is a mismatch between the service type chosen and the provider designation on file. A lymphatic drainage session, for example, is claimed as massage therapy when a registered massage therapist provides it, because claim systems sort by profession rather than by treatment name. Choose the profession, and keep the receipt that shows it.</p>

          <h2>Find care that fits your Green Shield plan</h2>
          <p>Look at the profession first, then the treatment. Browse the <a href="/#directory">WellFinder directory</a> to compare clinics across Canada, and open pages such as <a href="/clinics-facial-manual-therapy">facial manual therapy clinics</a> and <a href="/clinics-lymphatic-drainage">lymphatic drainage clinics</a> to see providers and how their visits bill. Before you book, sign in to GreenShield+ to confirm the category and balance, and ask the clinic whether it can bill Green Shield directly.</p>
          <p>WellFinder is an independent directory and is not affiliated with Green Shield Canada. This guide explains common features of Green Shield group plans in Canada. Your employer plan governs your coverage, and Green Shield or your plan administrator can confirm what your plan pays.</p>

